    "body": "### Problem\n\nwhen navigating up/down in directory parents, user has to find the place where they came from.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n- when using `-` to go to a parent dir, the cursor should be placed on the originating file/dir.\n    - impl note: should be just a `vim.fn.search()` call hopefully.\n- after going \"up\" multiple times, user can follow the path back to original file just by hitting `<enter>` multiple times.\n    - this should \"just work\" because Nvim buffers remember the cursor position; it shouldn't require any code to support this \"reverse\" flow.\n\n\ncc @barrettruth ",
